---
title: The Darkmown Blog
description: Notes on shipping Markdown that runs — collections, feeds, drafts, and zero-JS releases. This whole index is one @loop over a folder.
image: https://darkmown.com/__wd/media/og.png
transitions: true
---

@include /nav.wd
@include /base.wd

<main class="wide app-blog">

<header class="blog-head">
  <span class="eyebrow">The Darkmown Blog</span>

# Notes from the framework

Every post below is a plain `.md` file in `site/pages/blog/`. This page is **one
`@loop` over that folder** — sorted newest-first, paginated, and 100% static
HTML. No hand-maintained list, no config, no JavaScript.

</header>

<section class="post-list">

@loop blog into post sort by post.date desc paginate 3
::: card .post-card
::: post-meta
<time>{ post.date }</time>
@loop post.tags into tag
<span class="tag">{ tag }</span>
@endloop
:::

### [{ post.title }]({ post.url })

::: post-excerpt
{ post.excerpt }
:::

::: post-more
[Read post → ]({ post.url })
:::
:::
@empty
::: empty-note
No posts yet. Add a dated `.md` file to `site/pages/blog/`.
:::
@endloop

</section>

::: pager
::: pager-side
:if page.prev
[← Newer posts]({ page.prev }){.pager-link}
:endif
:::

::: pager-now
Page { page.current } of { page.total }
:::

::: pager-side .pager-side--end
:if page.next
[Older posts →]({ page.next }){.pager-link}
:endif
:::
:::

</main>

@include /footer.wd
